module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_width_constrained_integer_admits_a_value_outside_its_width

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread, BlockerClassUnstated }

data a_width_constrained_integer_admits_a_value_outside_its_width: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_width_constrained_integer_admits_a_value_outside_its_width" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value typed by a width-constrained integer (std.integer UInt8..UInt128, Int8..Int128: Compose<carrier, MachineWidth<N>>) that is not in [0, 2^N) (unsigned) or [-2^(N-1), 2^(N-1)) (signed). HARM: silent wrongness at the declared type -- a literal 300 at UInt8, or 255 + 1 typed UInt8, is accepted and evaluated as an ordinary Int, so the interpreted and emitted realizations of one program disagree and nothing said the width was crossed. THE CROSSING RULE is gunbc.design_ruling coercion_is_the_implicit_safe_subset (DESIGN section 4), applied to widths by sleek-owl-397 on 2026-10-25 and relayed by tidy-ant-251. A width is a checked refinement on Int and stays a bound (Compose<Int, MachineWidth<N>>), not a nominal brand. Narrowing into a width is a named, checked route. Widening that keeps signedness is implicit, because it is total, exact, unique, pure and consent-free, provided every widening chain along the one MachineWidth axis denotes the same value; if two routes disagree, the coercion refuses. A change of signedness (UInt8 -> Int8, Int8 -> UInt16) is not widening and is a named route. Wrapping exists only as a named operation. WITHDRAWN: this row previously stated an operator ruling of no implicit narrowing or widening; neither tidy-ant-251 nor sleek-owl-397 could source one (2026-10-25), so the widening half had no authority and is replaced by the rule above. This row is the width-specific face of bounded_natural_arithmetic_evaluated_as_unbounded_int, which keeps the arithmetic history; it is separate because the literal boundary, the arithmetic boundary and the carrier boundary climb on different triggers.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: Compose is a Phantom and transparent to Int at a formal, so no check at a call or return consults N; the class is not an overflow of the host Int (that refuses) but a missing refusal at the DECLARED width. THREE BOUNDARIES, kept apart because a rung is the minimum across them: (1) LITERAL -- an Int literal at a width position; (2) ARITHMETIC -- infix + - * on a width operand and the word32_* family that routes it; (3) CARRIER -- a non-literal Int reaching a width formal or field.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent wrongness) on all three boundaries. RUNG NOW, BOUNDARY (1) ONLY (A0-2): a located, typed refusal at infer -- v2.compiler.infer infer_int_literal_value_at reads Compose<A, MachineWidth<N>> and refuses a literal outside std.machine_width_range machine_width_admits with infer_reason_literal_outside_machine_width -- mitigation by a refusal that is loud and located, not construction, because a non-literal Int still reaches the same formal unchecked. Boundaries (2) and (3) are unchanged. SUBJECT GRAIN OF THE EVIDENCE: two grains, both executed. (a) PEERS: claims that restate std.integer's Int, UInt, UInt8 and Int8 declarations as it writes them. (b) THE REAL CLOSURE: v2.test.claim.compiler.width_literal_admission_real assembles the 28-module std.integer closure and infers a call at the real UInt8 formal -- 255 is admitted, 300 draws infer_reason_literal_outside_machine_width, and the same program without the call is accepted. Measured finding that made (b) possible: infer unfolded std.machine_constraints Compose (type Compose<A, M> = Phantom) as a transparent alias, so every literal at the real UInt8 formal, 255 included, was refused application_argument_does_not_inhabit before the width was read; infer_type_alias_unfolded_at now leaves Compose folded (its revert arm turns the real-closure 255 claim red). The rung for boundary (1) is therefore established at the real-closure grain for UInt8 literals; Int8 and the other widths are covered at peer grain only",
    "CEILING, WITH REASON: structurally impossible at the carrier -- a sole-constructed width carrier whose range admission (std.machine_width_range machine_width_admits) is its only mint, so an out-of-width value has no constructor. std.machine_word Word is the value-level carrier (the earlier std.bounded_nat family was deleted as a second carrier with no production consumer; its checked operations are std.machine_word word_checked_*). Decidable and fully modeled, hence reachable; not undecidable, so not a ratchet. RESIDUAL HONESTY: Word is not sole_constructor today (word_qualified proves a Word after the fact), so the carrier boundary's ceiling is not yet reached.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, AT CAPABILITY GRAIN: (2) the crypto word fold (sha1/sha2/png over the Int word32_* kernels) and any infix arithmetic on a width operand reach std.machine_word word_checked_* or a named wrapping operation, SUFFICIENT FOR no unchecked Int arithmetic to remain on a width-typed value; (3) a width carrier with sole construction exists and the Compose sole_constructor handling in the infer lane admits its mint, SUFFICIENT FOR a non-literal Int to be refused at a width formal. BOUNDARY (3) IS NOT STALLED. A stall recorded here deferred it only so that two lanes would not edit load-bearing infer at once; tidy-ant-251 released it on 2026-10-25, because #14087 no longer touches infer. A width formal admitting any non-literal Int is a correctness gap below ceiling. Rung now: BELOW the ladder for boundary (3): a non-literal Int at a width formal bypasses word_of_int and is silently admitted. Mitigation holds only for callers of the mint (std.machine_word word_of_int refuses there). Ceiling: structurally impossible (Word sole_constructor, word_of_int its only mint). Trigger: v2.compiler.infer sees Compose through a sealed head (the sole_constructor-erases-structure gap-analysis row). Owner: the machine-width carrier program (S1a gunbc#15110, one derivation of a width reading; S1b, extents and the ten width rows, after std.measure's Measure binders are kinded). The infer wall is keen-heron-809's, cleared per stage. The Compose-literal trigger previously named here is discharged (see the grain sentence above). The discriminating controls are width_literal_admission (peers) and width_literal_admission_real (real closure): 300 at UInt8 refuses, 255 at UInt8 is admitted; and for the arithmetic boundary test.claim.machine_word_witness checked_add_of_255_and_1_at_width8_overflows / wrapping_add_of_255_and_1_at_width8_is_zero.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.machine_width_range", decl_name: "machine_width_admits", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.width_literal_admission", decl_name: "wla_uint8_300_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.width_literal_admission", decl_name: "wla_uint8_255_is_admitted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.width_literal_admission_real", decl_name: "wlr_real_uint8_300_refuses_at_the_width", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.width_literal_admission_real", decl_name: "wlr_real_uint8_255_is_admitted", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
